        quiz: { questions: [{ question: "What is the most important reason for young adults to have basic estate planning documents, even if they don't have significant assets?", options: ["To minimize estate taxes on their wealth", "To ensure their wishes are known and legally documented, and to designate decision-makers if they become incapacitated", "To qualify for government benefits and programs", "To impress potential romantic partners with their responsibility"], correctAnswer: "To ensure their wishes are known and legally documented, and to designate decision-makers if they become incapacitated", explanation: "Even young adults with modest assets need estate planning to ensure their wishes are documented and to designate trusted people to make financial and medical decisions if they become incapacitated. This provides protection and peace of mind regardless of wealth level." }] },
